 "useCases": [
  {
   "description": "I'm a seller on Ozon (Russian Amazon), and I develop some applications for inside usage. Like, forming supplies, etc. I've got sheets of barcodes stickers printed without labels, and to not confuse them, I have to scan them before applying. Not each, but at least one from every sheet. Same with supplies: supply sticker has a barcode, and absolutely no information about the supply contents. \nI want to make an application that'll at least tell me the barcode itself, the leftover stock, the supplies related with it, and if I scan a supply barcode - then the supply details. \nOr, for orders: order barcodes are just a label with a QR-code and a order number. It would be nice if I can scan and check it through my app/system. \n\nOn mobile systems, it would make a great api.\nOn desktop, it could help with developing a \"qr scanner\" extension, with UI like the screenshot feature in Firefox.",
   "url": "https://github.com/web-platform-dx/developer-signals/issues/121#issuecomment-6311756871"
  }
 ],
